The ARMv7 cache-maintenance and Linux handoff sequence is derived from the
Project Cascadia A5 staging loader:

  https://github.com/rzxvx/Project-Cascadia
  reference revision: 091d441f19e101699f7e1835a80ccb48d6e54eec
  license: GPL-2.0

The local P105 work fixed the executable entry by discarding ARM unwind
metadata and asserting the upload address in the linker script.

This producer keeps those entry safeguards. Hardware addresses come from
the device's profile. Orchard's configuration record and DTB editor add
bounded external-initramfs placement; that extension requires a fresh
hardware boot before it is described as working.
